<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Model Parameters</h2>

<figure id="A1.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Hyperparameters of our <math id="A1.T5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u_{s}^{{\bm{\theta}}}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{s}^{{\bm{\theta}}}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math> model shared across all datasets.</figcaption>
<table id="A1.T5.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A1.T5.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Parameter</td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Value</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Number of <math id="A1.T5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ins" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ins</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ins</annotation></semantics></math> bins <math id="A1.T5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{\text{ins}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mtext>ins</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{\text{ins}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">64</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Number of <math id="A1.T5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sub" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>sub</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sub</annotation></semantics></math> bins <math id="A1.T5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{\text{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mtext>sub</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{\text{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">64</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Maximum <math id="A1.T5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sub" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>sub</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sub</annotation></semantics></math> distance <math id="A1.T5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><math id="A1.T5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nicefrac{{T}}{{100}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mi mathsize="0.700em">T</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nicefrac{{T}}{{100}}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Maximum log-rate <math id="A1.T5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>M</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{M}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">32</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A1.T5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><math id="A1.T5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-{\cos\big(\frac{\pi}{2}s\big)}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-{\cos\big(\frac{\pi}{2}s\big)}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" colspan="2"><span id="A1.T5.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Llama architecture:</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">   Hidden size <math id="A1.T5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">64</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">   Layers</td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">2</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">   Attention heads</td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">4</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Optimizer</td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Adam</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.12" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Sample steps</td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">100</td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All <span title="multi-layer perceptron" class="ltx_glossaryref">MLPs</span> have input and output sizes of <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, except for the final <span title="multi-layer perceptron" class="ltx_glossaryref">MLP</span> whose output size is determined by the number of <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> parameters of the rate.
The <span title="multi-layer perceptron" class="ltx_glossaryref">MLPs</span> have a single hidden layer of size <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4H</annotation></semantics></math>.
The sinusoidal embeddings map a scalar <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> to a vector of length <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>.
In contrast to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Havasi et al. (2025)</a></cite>, we choose a cosine <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> schedule <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(s)=1-{\cos\big(\frac{\pi}{2}s\big)}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(s)=1-{\cos\big(\frac{\pi}{2}s\big)}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nichol &amp; Dhariwal (2021)</a></cite> for diffusion models as it improved results slightly compared <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(s)=s^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(s)=s^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For evaluation, we use an <span title="exponential moving average" class="ltx_glossaryref">exponential moving average (EMA)</span> of the model weights.
We also use low-discrepancy sampling of <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S3.E14" title="In 3.3 Training ‣ 3 Method ‣ Edit-Based Flow Matching for Temporal Point Processes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> during training to smooth the loss and thus training signal <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kingma et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lienen et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We train all models for <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20\,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20 000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20\,000</annotation></semantics></math> steps and select the best checkpoint by its <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-over-<math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{IET}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>IET</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{IET}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which we evaluate on a validation set every <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1000</annotation></semantics></math> steps.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Metrics</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A standard way in generative modeling to compare generated and real data is the Wasserstein distance <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Heusel et al., 2017</a>)</cite>.
It is the minimum average distance between elements of the two datasets under the optimal (partial) assignment between them,</p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{p}(\mathcal{X},\mathcal{X}^{\prime})={\Big(\min\nolimits_{\gamma\in\Gamma(\mathcal{X},\mathcal{X}^{\prime})}\E\nolimits_{({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\sim\gamma}\,\big[{d({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})}^{p}\big]\Big)}^{\nicefrac{{1}}{{p}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mi mathsize="0.710em">p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{p}(\mathcal{X},\mathcal{X}^{\prime})={\Big(\min\nolimits_{\gamma\in\Gamma(\mathcal{X},\mathcal{X}^{\prime})}\E\nolimits_{({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\sim\gamma}\,\big[{d({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})}^{p}\big]\Big)}^{\nicefrac{{1}}{{p}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is a distance that compares elements from the two sets.
In the case of sequences of unequal length, one can choose <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> itself as a nested Wasserstein distance <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lienen et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiao et al. (2017)</a></cite> were the first to design such a distance between <span title="temporal point process" class="ltx_glossaryref">TPPs</span>.
They exploit a special case of <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> for sorted sequences of equal length and assign the remaining events of the longer sequence to pseudo-events at <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> to define</p>
<table id="A2.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{Xiao}}({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=\sum\nolimits_{i=1}^{|{\bm{x}}|}|t^{(i)}-t^{\prime(i)}|+\sum\nolimits_{i=|{\bm{x}}|+1}^{|{\bm{x}}^{\prime}|}|T-t^{\prime(i)}|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>Xiao</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{Xiao}}({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=\sum\nolimits_{i=1}^{|{\bm{x}}|}|t^{(i)}-t^{\prime(i)}|+\sum\nolimits_{i=|{\bm{x}}|+1}^{|{\bm{x}}^{\prime}|}|T-t^{\prime(i)}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is assumed to be the longer sequence.
<math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{Xiao}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>Xiao</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{Xiao}}</annotation></semantics></math> captures a difference in both location and number of events between two sequences through its two terms.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shchur et al., 2020b</a>)</cite> propose to compute the <span title="maximum mean discrepancy" class="ltx_glossaryref">MMD</span> between sets based on a Gaussian kernel and <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{Xiao}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>Xiao</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{Xiao}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In addition, we evaluate the event count distributions via a Wasserstein-1 distance with respect to a difference in event counts <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1,d_{l}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1,d_{l}}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{l}({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=\big||{\bm{x}}|-|{\bm{x}}^{\prime}|\big|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{l}({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=\big||{\bm{x}}|-|{\bm{x}}^{\prime}|\big|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, we the distributions of inter-event times between our generated sequences and real sequences in <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1,d_{\mathrm{IET}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>IET</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1,d_{\mathrm{IET}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., a Wasserstein-1 distance of <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{IET}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>IET</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{IET}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{IET}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>IET</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{IET}}</annotation></semantics></math> is itself the <math id="A2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> distance between inter-event times of two sequences and quantifies how adjacent events relate to each other to capture more complex patterns.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Detailed Results</h2>

